Price units differ between the two sources
-------------------------------------------------------------------
litellm states prices PER TOKEN (`input_cost_per_token`,
`output_cost_per_token`); models.dev states them PER MILLION TOKENS
(`cost.input`, `cost.output`). The derived cache MULTIPLIERS divide two
fields from the same source, so their units cancel; the baked base rates
do not, and the generator normalizes models.dev to per-token before
cross-checking the two sources. Keep this in mind when reading a
disagreement reported by the generator: both values in its message are
already per-token.

cross_check_allowlist.json
-------------------------------------------------------------------
Not vendored data -- a routectl-authored file recording the specific
(selector, field) pairs where the two sources above disagree and which
value the generator uses, with a rationale. See that file for the
current entries.

Refreshing the snapshots
-------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Re-fetch both URLs above, overwrite the two JSON files in this
   directory, and update the snapshot dates here.
2. Update `CATALOG_SNAPSHOT_DATE` in `../src/catalog_codegen.rs` to match.
3. Run `cargo run --bin gen_catalog` from the workspace root (or this
   crate) to regenerate `../src/catalog_baked.rs`.
4. Bump `CATALOG_VERSION` in `../src/catalog_codegen.rs` if the output
   changed materially (rows added/removed, derivation rules changed) --
   not on every refresh with an unchanged shape.
5. Run `cargo fmt` and `cargo test -p routectl-router` (the drift-guard
   test fails if the checked-in file is stale).
